<title>USA: Portland General Q4 oper net rises.</title>
<headline>Portland General Q4 oper net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>PORTLAND GENERAL CORP</p>
<p> THREE-MONTHS ENDED DEC 31		  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		    $317,719     $281,901</p>
<p> Operating Expenses(a)		  219,458	205,768</p>
<p> Net Operating Income		    72,806	 58,578</p>
<p> Net Income				  25,954	 36,406</p>
<p> Ag shrs				 51,243,669   50,967,781</p>
<p> Earnings Per Average Common Share     0.51	   0.71</p>
<p> YEAR ENDED DEC 31			    1996	  1995</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		  $1,111,816     $983,582</p>
<p> Operating Expenses(a)		  770,739	698,942</p>
<p> Net Operating Income		   235,967	195,576</p>
<p> Regulatory Disallowances(b)		  -     (49,567)</p>
<p> Net Income				 129,536	 81,036</p>
<p> Avg shrs				51,144,462   50,766,916</p>
<p>(a)  Excluding income taxes</p>
<p>(b)  Net of income taxes of $25,542</p>
<p>	   (All Data Above 000s Except Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Fourth quarter earnings include a $13 million or $.25 per share after tax charge for merger related costs.</p>
<p>Earnings for the 12 months ended December 31, 1996. period include an $18.2 million, or $.36 per share after tax charge for costs related to the proposed merger with Enron.</p>
</text>
